WEBVTT

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:31.086
And as Luz found, it doesn't
have to be a group of peers.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.202
Now she could connect
and share her interest

00:17:33.226 --> 00:17:34.769
in Puerto Rican cultural events

00:17:34.793 --> 00:17:36.076
with others at work,

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:37.967
like when a hurricane hit Puerto Rico

00:17:37.991 --> 00:17:41.796
and Luz was hosting visiting interns
whose universities had closed down.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.816
LC: They were missing home a lot.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:48.466
And if I knew of a concert
of music from Puerto Rico,

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.206
I would invite them there.

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:55.446
And so I think that served to help
to give them a sense of belonging

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:56.826
that maybe they don't have,

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:58.996
you know, in the everyday, in the work.

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:02.278
AG: Is this something that you've done
when you're feeling lonely?